{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>עַל דְּבַר שָׂרַי אֵשֶׁת אַבְרָם — on account of Sarai the wife of Abram.</b> But do we not yet know that Sarai was the wife of Abram? And furthermore, what was Pharaoh's offense — did he not suppose she was his sister? And as for what Rashi explained, that 'עַל דְּבַר שָׂרַי' means that she would say to the angel, 'Strike!' and he would strike — the word 'strike' is not mentioned in the verse. Therefore it appears to me that although before the multitude Sarah said, 'I am his sister,' nevertheless to Pharaoh she told the truth, that she was Abram's wife, reckoning that a king who sits on a throne of justice would not commit wrongdoing. But Pharaoh paid no heed to her, for he said, 'To your earlier words I give credence.' Therefore HaShem struck 'עַל דְּבַר שָׂרַי — on account of the matter of Sarai' — on account of Sarai's own speech. And what was her speech? 'אֵשֶׁת אַבְרָם — the wife of Abram' — for she had spoken to him, 'I am the wife of Abram.' And Pharaoh said to Abram, 'לָמָּה אָמַרְתָּ אֲחֹתִי הִיא — Why did you say, She is my sister?' (Genesis 12:18), for 'to you I would have believed and not to her, for I thought: perhaps she says this in order to escape the lying with her that is without marriage.' Another matter: 'עַל דְּבַר שָׂרַי אֵשֶׁת אַבְרָם — on account of Sarai the wife of Abram' — because she was a married woman's wife, therefore these plagues came upon him."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:28:08.167052027Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}